    "did_you_know": "At age 12, Ana Mendieta was sent from Cuba to live in the United States in 1961 after the Communists took control of the island.",
    "description": "“I have been carrying out a dialogue between the landscape and the female body (based on my own silhouette),” wrote Mendieta. “I believe this has been a direct result of my having been torn from my homeland (Cuba) during my adolescence.” Sculpting into the soil at the edge of a slope, Mendieta created a silhouette based on her own body. She then photographed that ephemeral earth work. The photograph is the part of the artwork that remains.",
